# Copy to vision.env (git-ignored) and edit. gateway/run.sh loads it by itself when it
# starts (set VISION_ENV_FILE to use another file); its values replace same-named
# variables already set in your shell. Changes take effect on the next run.sh.
# Nothing here is required: every value shown is the default.

# Where Python environments, model weights, jobs and the job database live.
# Must be on storage that every Slurm compute node can read and write.
# Default: a "vision-data" folder next to the repository.
# VISION_DATA_DIR=/path/to/vision-data

# Hugging Face token. Needed only to download gated weights
# (LTX-2.5: see models/ltx25/download_weights.sh).
# HF_TOKEN=

# Gateway
# MODEL_API_HOST=0.0.0.0
# The port is always 8012 (gateway/run.sh ignores MODEL_API_PORT).
# MODEL_API_FALLBACK_PARTITION=background
# MODEL_API_SLURM_JOB_NAME_PREFIX=data-validation-
# Everything about a job (logs, inputs, outputs, request) is kept for this many
# days after it finishes. A request sent with "incognito": true (the web UI's
# Incognito switch) is the exception: nothing of it is kept longer than needed.
# MODEL_API_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# An upload that no job references is deleted this many minutes after upload.
# MODEL_API_UNUSED_UPLOAD_TTL_MINUTES=60
# The global GPU limit and each model's limit on concurrent jobs (= warm workers) are not set here: change them
# while the gateway runs, on the "GPU capacity" page of the web UI.
# Most jobs one warm-pool backend (Qwen-Image-2.1, H3, ACE-Step 1.5, Stable Audio Open, Stable Audio 3, YuE2,
# Parakeet, Breeze TTS) or
# Qwen3.8 may have queued or running at once; a request beyond that is refused with 429.
# MODEL_API_MAX_QUEUED_PER_BACKEND=1000
# Most times one such job is started in total: a job whose worker (or the Qwen3.8 server) was lost, for example
# pre-empted, is queued again until it has been started this many times. Model errors are never retried.
# MODEL_API_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3

# MiniMax H3 (see docs/models/h3/README.md). Every job holds 4 or 8 GPUs on one
# node and always denoises in "ulysses" mode; the gateway sizes each request from
# its prompt, references and video length, and refuses one that does not fit (422).
# All of these are initial guesses, to be refitted from the usage log
# (<data dir>/metrics/h3_jobs.jsonl). gateway/run.sh reads them when it starts.
# GPU counts a job may be given, smallest first. "4" pins every job to four GPUs.
# H3_GPU_OPTIONS=4,8
# Most rows of the denoising sequence one GPU may hold, and most tokens the text encoder may read.
# H3_ROWS_PER_GPU=40000
# H3_MAX_ENCODER_TOKENS=60000
# Slurm shape: memory for the whole job, CPUs per GPU, and the longest a job (and so an estimate) may be.
# H3_MEM=256G
# H3_CPUS_PER_GPU=8
# H3_API_TIME=01:30:00
# Warm workers: a request is run by one of the long-lived jobs (4 or 8 GPUs each; how many may run is H3's limit on the
# GPU capacity page), so only the first request on a worker reads the weights from shared storage. A worker idle this
# long is stopped. WORKER_TIME is the Slurm time limit of a worker and must be longer than H3_API_TIME.
# H3_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# H3_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00
# Attention backend for the transformer; set to an empty string to use diffusers' default (about 2x slower).
# H3_ATTENTION_BACKEND=_flash_3_hub

# Qwen-Image-2.1 (see docs/models/qwen_image21/README.md). Requests are run by long-lived one-GPU workers that
# load a checkpoint once (how many may run is its limit on the GPU capacity page); a worker idle for
# IDLE_MINUTES is stopped. JOB_TIME is the longest one request may run, WORKER_TIME the Slurm time limit
# of a worker (it must be longer). gateway/run.sh passes IDLE_MINUTES and WORKER_TIME on to the gateway.
# QWEN_IMAGE21_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# QWEN_IMAGE21_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00

# Music backends (see docs/models/ace_step15, stable_audio_open, stable_audio3, yue2). Each has its own warm workers:
# one-GPU jobs that load the model once; a worker idle for IDLE_MINUTES is stopped. WORKER_TIME is the Slurm time
# limit of a worker. gateway/run.sh passes these two variables of each backend on to the gateway. How many workers
# each may run is set on the GPU capacity page.
# ACE_STEP15_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# ACE_STEP15_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00
# STABLE_AUDIO_OPEN_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# STABLE_AUDIO_OPEN_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00
# STABLE_AUDIO3_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# STABLE_AUDIO3_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00
# YUE2_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# YUE2_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00

# Parakeet (speech to text) and Breeze TTS (text to speech) work the same way: one-GPU warm workers, each
# stopped after IDLE_MINUTES without a request. gateway/run.sh passes these two variables of each on.
# PARAKEET_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# PARAKEET_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00
# BREEZE_TTS_IDLE_MINUTES=10
# BREEZE_TTS_WORKER_TIME=12:00:00

# Qwen3.8 text model (see docs/models/qwen38/README.md). One shared vLLM server on one
# GPU, started by the first request and stopped after it has been idle for a while.
# gateway/run.sh passes every QWEN38_* variable on to the gateway.
# Partition for the server. Unset uses the fallback partition, which can pre-empt it (the server is then restarted
# by the next request). Set a non-pre-emptible partition for steady use.
# QWEN38_PARTITION=
# Minutes without a request after which the server stops itself.
# QWEN38_IDLE_MINUTES=20
# Slurm shape of the server job.
# QWEN38_MEM_PER_GPU=64G
# QWEN38_CPUS=8
# QWEN38_SERVER_TIME=12:00:00
# Seconds a request may wait for the server to start, and for its answer.
# QWEN38_STARTUP_TIMEOUT=1800
# QWEN38_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=1800
# Requests sent to the server at once.
# QWEN38_MAX_CONCURRENT=8
